  "question": {
    "text": "Amongst the following statements regarding adsorption, those that are valid are:<br />(a)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> becomes less negative as adsorption proceeds.<br />(b) On a given adsorbent, ammonia is adsorbed more than nitrogen gas.<br />(c) On adsorption, the residual force acting along the surface of the adsorbent increases<br />(d) With increase in temperature, the equilibrium concentration of adsorbate increases.",
    "image": null
  },
